{"role":"assistant","content":"Syntax and plist are valid. Now the behavioral simulation.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_t6kixxBE556d5wBi9CtzaGoQ","function":{"name":"Bash","arguments":"{\"command\":\"set -u\\nroot=\\\"$PWD\\\"\\nscratch=\\\"$root/.verify\\\"\\nrm -rf \\\"$scratch\\\"; mkdir -p \\\"$scratch/home/projects/shop\\\" \\\"$scratch/home/bin\\\" \\\"$scratch/home/Library/Logs\\\"\\n\\n# fake claude: fails like the real one did while $HOME/.claude-fail exists, otherwise succeeds\\ncat > \\\"$scratch/home/bin/claude\\\" <<'EOF'\\n#!/bin/bash\\nprompt=$(cat)\\nif [ -f \\\"$HOME/.claude-fail\\\" ]; then\\n  echo \\\"Not logged in · Please run /login\\\" >&2\\n  exit 1\\nfi\\nprintf '%s\\\\n' \\\"$prompt\\\" > \\\"$HOME/got-prompt.txt\\\"\\necho \\\"Fake review: 1 commit, nothing risky.\\\"\\necho \\\"Summary one\\\"; echo \\\"Summary two\\\"; echo \\\"Summary three\\\"\\nexit 0\\nEOF\\n\\n# fake notify: records instead of hitting Telegram (ground rules: no external services)\\ncat > \\\"$scratch/home/bin/notify.sh\\\" <<'EOF'\\n#!/bin/bash\\necho \\\"$1\\\" >> \\\"$HOME/sent.log\\\"\\nEOF\\nchmod +x \\\"$scratch/home/bin/claude\\\" \\\"$scratch/home/bin/notify.sh\\\"\\n\\ngit -C \\\"$scratch/home/projects/shop\\\" init -q\\ngit -C \\\"$scratch/home/projects/shop\\\" -c user.email=t@t -c user.name=t commit -q --allow-empty -m test\\n\\nrun() { # $1=script $2=label\\n  local rc\\n  env -i PATH=\\\"$scratch/home/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\\\" HOME=\\\"$scratch/home\\\" USER=vk \\\\\\n    /bin/zsh \\\"$1\\\" > \\\"$scratch/$2.stdout\\\" 2> \\\"$scratch/$2.stderr\\\"\\n  rc=$?\\n  echo \\\"== $2: exit=$rc ==\\\"\\n  echo \\\"-- stderr:\\\"; cat \\\"$scratch/$2.stderr\\\"\\n}\\n\\n# Run A: ORIGINAL script (from git) with failing claude — expect reproduction of the bug\\ngit show HEAD:bin/nightly-review.zsh > \\\"$scratch/orig.zsh\\\"\\ntouch \\\"$scratch/home/.claude-fail\\\"\\nrun \\\"$scratch/orig.zsh\\\" A-orig-failing\\necho